      "stageRecord": "Merge embedded T and raise the complex v head to it. T agrees with Ana and values nominative Case, after which Ana undergoes Internal Merge to the preverbal subject position. Both movements have sources in the preceding workspace. Merge que as subordinate C, then merge Quiero with the resulting finite CP. Adjoin mañana to this matrix verbal predicate before merging matrix v and its silent first-person singular subject pro. Thus mañana modifies the wanting, while the CP specifies what is wanted. The desiderative verb licenses subjunctive mood in its finite complement. Whole-word venga is pronounced at its highest head occurrence; silent T contributes no separate overt terminal.",
